0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                             ;  B8Script interpreter for the Motorola 6809
0000                             ;  Spec: docs/b8script.md (2026-10-09) plus the 2026-11-20 changes:
0000                             ;        [x stores in a variable, "[ " pushes an anonymous block, any other
0000                             ;        character after [ is an error, the heap pointer lives at z10+.
0000                             ;        The string escape is "/" (it was ">").
0000                             ;        "/" leaves ( r q ), the quotient on top; dividing by zero is not
0000                             ;        checked. -n? does no more editing than Backspace.
0000                             ;  Follows the design of the Z80 interpreter (z80/b8s-z80.asm).
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Two builds, selected by the CHECKED line below (CPM is always 0: the 6809
0000                             ;  has no CP/M; the line is kept only so that build.sh works):
0000                             ;    CHECKED  0 = no checks (spec: "B8Script checks nothing")
0000                             ;             1 = stops on stack overrun, Ctrl-C, heap past the limit, a store
0000                             ;                 outside the program's own space, and a bad character after [,
0000                             ;                 printing a letter and the place, like  S @ 245
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Assembler: asm80, M6809 mode.
0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                CPM:      EQU   0   ; always 0 (no CP/M on the 6809)
0000                CHECKED:   EQU   1   ; 1 = checked build
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ;  Register use, everywhere in the interpreter
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;    Y    IP: the address of the next program character to read
0000                             ;    U    the data stack pointer. The stack grows down and U points at the
0000                             ;         top cell (TOS); nothing is cached in a register, because every
0000                             ;         dispatch needs A, B and X as scratch. Cells are big-endian here.
0000                             ;         (Only the stacks are big-endian: cells in RAM that the program can
0000                             ;         see - variables, the heap pointer, anything @ and ! reach - are
0000                             ;         little-endian, as the spec says, so @ and ! swap the bytes.)
0000                             ;    S    the return stack. A word call is a plain push of Y. Entries are
0000                             ;         2 bytes, big-endian. Handlers are called with JSR, so the return
0000                             ;         address of the dispatcher is on top of S while a handler runs.
0000                             ;    DP   the letter page, so the letter-page variables below cost 2-byte
0000                             ;         direct addressing. Nothing else may change DP.
0000                             ;    A B X are scratch. Every handler is entered by JSR and ends in RTS (one
0000                             ;    byte). A handler that pushes or pops the return stack first pulls the
0000                             ;    dispatcher's return address into X (PULS X) and ends with JMP ,X.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Dispatch (unchecked build). PTAB holds one byte per punctuation character:
0000                             ;  the low byte of the handler's distance from PTAB. The handlers of the last
0000                             ;  characters (in code order) start within 256 bytes after PTAB, the handlers
0000                             ;  of the first NPG1 characters in the 256 bytes after that. The assembler
0000                             ;  works NPG1 out from where five handlers landed, and testing/chktab09.py
0000                             ;  checks the layout. The checked build is bigger than that reach, so its
0000                             ;  table holds whole addresses instead.
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ;  Memory map. Everything the interpreter writes is in four RAM areas:
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;    8000h-80FFh  return stack, 127 entries; empty = 8100h; S stays inside
0000                             ;    8100h-81FFh  data stack, 127 cells; empty = 8200h; U stays inside
0000                             ;    8200h-82FFh  letter page (LET): A..Z at +00h..+33h, a..z at +40h..+73h
0000                             ;                 (a word cell is always 64 bytes below its variable), the
0000                             ;                 heap pointer at +7Ch (= z10+), interpreter variables in the
0000                             ;                 gaps, and the -n? line buffer at +80h..+FFh
0000                             ;    8300h-       PROG, the program text, NUL-terminated; the heap starts
0000                             ;                 after the NUL and grows to HEAPLIM*256 (F000h)
0000                             ;    F000h-       this image (ROM). The reset vector (FFFEh) must point to
0000                             ;                 `start` (see the listing); the image does not contain it.
0000                             ;    FF03h-FF0Bh  the console routines (CONOUT, KEY) and EXIT are supplied
0000                             ;                 by the system and need no space here.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  The stacks sit below the letter page, so "the program's own space" (what
0000                             ;  the checked build lets ! and . write) is the single range LET..HEAPLIM*256.
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ; ---- generic machine: edit these to suit -----------------------------------
0000                KEY:      EQU   0FF06h   ; a waiting key in A, or A = 0 if none is
0000                             ;   waiting. The Z flag must match A (end the
0000                             ;   routine with TSTA / RTS, or a plain LDA).
0000                CONOUT:   EQU   0FF03h   ; print the character in A
0000                EXIT:     EQU   0FF09h   ; where to go when the program ends
0000                             ;   Both are called with JSR. They may change A and CC and must preserve
0000                             ;   B, X, Y, U and DP.
0000                RSPAGE:   EQU   80h   
0000                DSPAGE:   EQU   81h   
0000                LETPAGE:   EQU   82h   
0000                PROG:     EQU   8300h   ; where the loader puts the program text
0000                HEAPLIM:   EQU   0F0h   ; the heap must stay below F000h (a page)
0000                MSLOOP:   EQU   20   ; n? inner loop count for about 1 ms; tune it
0000                             ; for your clock and your KEY routine
0000                             ; letter-page layout (direct-page offsets inside LETPAGE)
0000                LET:      EQU   LETPAGE*256   
0000                HEAP:     EQU   7Ch   ; z10+, the heap pointer (little-endian)
0000                KEYBUF:   EQU   34h   ; gap after Z: a key held back by the break check
0000                LINEBUF:   EQU   LET+80h   ; -n? text, ending in CR
0000                RSTOP:    EQU   RSPAGE*256+100h   ; empty return stack
0000                DSTOP:    EQU   DSPAGE*256+100h   ; empty data stack
F000                          .ORG   0F000h   
F000                             ; =============================================================================
F000                             ;  Checked build: the error report. It is here, ahead of the inner loop, so
F000                             ;  that the loop's stack checks reach it with short branches.
F000                             ; =============================================================================
F000                          IF   CHECKED   
F000                             ; Error entries. Each loads its letter and then hides the next entry inside
F000                             ; a 3-byte CMPX # (the 8Ch), so they all fall through to `error`.
F000   86 53        E_STACK:   LDA   #"S"   ; data stack over or under
F002   8C                     FCB   8Ch   
F003   86 52        E_RSTACK:   LDA   #"R"   ; return stack over or under
F005   8C                     FCB   8Ch   
F006   86 42        E_BREAK:   LDA   #"B"   ; Ctrl-C
F008   8C                     FCB   8Ch   
F009   86 48        E_HEAP:   LDA   #"H"   ; heap past the limit
F00B   8C                     FCB   8Ch   
F00C   86 57        E_STORE:   LDA   #"W"   ; write outside the program's space
F00E   8C                     FCB   8Ch   
F00F   86 44        E_BRACK:   LDA   #"D"   ; bad character after [
F011                             ; error: print the letter in A, " @ " and the offset in the program of the
F011                             ; character just read, then end. For example: S @ 245
F011   10 CE 81 00  ERROR:    LDS   #RSTOP   ; the stacks may be wrecked: start clean
F015   CE 82 00               LDU   #DSTOP   
F018   BD FF 03               JSR   CONOUT   
F01B   86 20                  LDA   #" "   
F01D   BD FF 03               JSR   CONOUT   
F020   86 40                  LDA   #"@"   
F022   BD FF 03               JSR   CONOUT   
F025   86 20                  LDA   #" "   
F027   BD FF 03               JSR   CONOUT   
F02A   1F 20                  TFR   Y,D   
F02C   83 83 01               SUBD   #PROG+1   ; the character just read
F02F   36 06                  PSHU   D   
F031   BD F2 DE               JSR   pdec   ; and fall into fin
F034                          ENDIF      
F034   7E FF 09     FIN:      JMP   EXIT   ; the program has ended
F037                             ; =============================================================================
F037                             ;  Startup
F037                             ; =============================================================================
F037   10 CE 81 00  START:    LDS   #RSTOP   
F03B   CE 82 00               LDU   #DSTOP   
F03E   86 82                  LDA   #LETPAGE   
F040   1F 8B                  TFR   A,DP   
F042   8E 83 00               LDX   #PROG   ; the heap starts after the program's NUL
F045   A6 80        SC:       LDA   ,X+   
F047   26 FC                  BNE   sc   
F049   1F 10                  TFR   X,D   
F04B   D7 7C                  STB   <HEAP   ; (little-endian)
F04D   97 7D                  STA   <HEAP+1   
F04F                          IF   CHECKED   
F04F   0F 34                  CLR   <KEYBUF   
F051                          ENDIF      
F051   10 8E 83 00            LDY   #PROG   
F055                             ; =============================================================================
F055                             ;  The inner loop: read one character and sort it by range.
F055                             ; 
F055                             ;    00h          end of program
F055                             ;    01h-20h, 7Fh-FFh   ignored (control, space, DEL, high bytes)
F055                             ;    30h-39h      digit: read a whole number
F055                             ;    41h-5Ah      A-Z: call the word in that letter's cell
F055                             ;    61h-7Ah      a-z: push the address of that letter's cell
F055                             ;    the rest     punctuation: JSR through PTAB, 32 entries, in code order
F055                             ; =============================================================================
F055                NEXT:        
F055                          IF   CHECKED   
F055                             ; Both stacks are checked once per character, not in every handler.
F055                             ; Each stack lives in one page, and "empty" is the first address of
F055                             ; the page above, so a stack is in range exactly when the address
F055                             ; one below its pointer is in the page (127 entries or cells).
F055   30 5F                  LEAX   -1,U   
F057   1F 10                  TFR   X,D   
F059   81 81                  CMPA   #DSPAGE   
F05B   26 A3                  BNE   e_stack   
F05D   30 7F                  LEAX   -1,S   
F05F   1F 10                  TFR   X,D   
F061   81 80                  CMPA   #RSPAGE   
F063   26 9E                  BNE   e_rstack   
F065                          ENDIF      
F065   A6 A0                  LDA   ,Y+   
F067   27 CB                  BEQ   fin   ; NUL ends the program
F069   80 21                  SUBA   #21h   ; A = c - 21h
F06B   25 E8                  BLO   next   ; 01h-20h ignored
F06D   81 0F                  CMPA   #0Fh   
F06F   25 22                  BLO   punct   ; 21h-2Fh: PTAB index 0-14
F071   80 0F                  SUBA   #0Fh   ; A = c - 30h
F073   81 0A                  CMPA   #0Ah   
F075   25 24                  BLO   digit   ; 30h-39h
F077   81 11                  CMPA   #11h   
F079   25 16                  BLO   p3a   ; 3Ah-40h
F07B   80 11                  SUBA   #11h   ; A = c - 41h
F07D   81 1A                  CMPA   #1Ah   
F07F   25 26                  BLO   upper   ; 41h-5Ah: A = letter index 0-25
F081   81 20                  CMPA   #20h   
F083   25 0A                  BLO   p5b   ; 5Bh-60h
F085   81 3A                  CMPA   #3Ah   
F087   25 18                  BLO   lower   ; 61h-7Ah: A = 20h-39h (cell +64 bytes)
F089   81 3E                  CMPA   #3Eh   
F08B   24 C8                  BHS   next   ; 7Fh-FFh: ignored
F08D   80 1A                  SUBA   #1Ah   ; 7Bh-7Eh: -1Eh in all, index 28-31
F08F   80 09        P5B:      SUBA   #9   ; 5Bh-60h: -4 in all, index 22-27
F091   8B 05        P3A:      ADDA   #5   ; 3Ah-40h: index 15-21
F093                             ; Punctuation: A = the PTAB index.
F093   8E F0 DF     PUNCT:    LDX   #PTAB   
F096                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                                 ; The handler is at PTAB + D, where B is the table byte and A is 1
                                 ; for the first NPG1 characters, 0 for the rest.
                              LDB   A,X   
                              CMPA   #NPG1   ; carry: one of the first NPG1
                              LDA   #0   ; (leaves the carry alone)
                              ROLA      
                              JSR   D,X   ; the handler ends in RTS
F096                          ENDIF      
F096                          IF   CHECKED   
F096   48                     ASLA      ; the table holds whole addresses
F097   AD 96                  JSR   [A,X]   
F099                          ENDIF      
F099   20 BA                  BRA   next   
F09B                             ; Digits: step back onto the first digit and read the whole number.
F09B   31 3F        DIGIT:    LEAY   -1,Y   
F09D   8D 22                  BSR   rdnum   
F09F   20 B4                  BRA   next   
F0A1                             ; a-z: push the cell's address (the cell is the variable)
F0A1   8D 10        LOWER:    BSR   cellx   
F0A3   36 10                  PSHU   X   
F0A5   20 AE                  BRA   next   
F0A7                             ; A-Z: call the word. The IP (the address after the letter) goes on the
F0A7                             ; return stack, and the IP becomes the address in the letter's cell.
F0A7   8D 0A        UPPER:    BSR   cellx   
F0A9   34 20                  PSHS   Y   
F0AB   E6 84                  LDB   ,X   
F0AD   A6 01                  LDA   1,X   
F0AF   1F 02                  TFR   D,Y   
F0B1   20 A2                  BRA   next   
F0B3                             ; cellx: A = letter index (0-25, or 32-57 for lowercase) -> X = cell address
F0B3   48           CELLX:    ASLA      
F0B4   8E 82 00               LDX   #LET   
F0B7   30 86                  LEAX   A,X   
F0B9   39                     RTS      
F0BA                             ; isdig: A = the character at IP minus "0"; the carry is set if it is a digit
F0BA   A6 A4        ISDIG:    LDA   ,Y   
F0BC   80 30                  SUBA   #"0"   
F0BE   81 0A                  CMPA   #10   
F0C0   39           AB9:      RTS      
F0C1                             ; rdnum: read decimal digits at IP and push the value; IP is left on the
F0C1                             ; first non-digit. Values wrap at 16 bits, as the spec says. The running
F0C1                             ; value lives in the new top cell: V = V*10 + digit.
F0C1   4F           RDNUM:    CLRA      
F0C2   5F                     CLRB      
F0C3   36 06                  PSHU   D   
F0C5   8D F3        RD1:      BSR   isdig   
F0C7   24 F7                  BHS   ab9   
F0C9   31 21                  LEAY   1,Y   
F0CB   34 02                  PSHS   A   
F0CD   EC C4                  LDD   ,U   
F0CF   58                     ASLB      
F0D0   49                     ROLA      
F0D1   58                     ASLB      
F0D2   49                     ROLA      
F0D3   E3 C4                  ADDD   ,U   ; 5V
F0D5   58                     ASLB      
F0D6   49                     ROLA      ; 10V
F0D7   EB E0                  ADDB   ,S+   
F0D9   89 00                  ADCA   #0   
F0DB   ED C4                  STD   ,U   
F0DD   20 E6                  BRA   rd1   
F0DF                             ; =============================================================================
F0DF                             ;  Dispatch table, in code order.
F0DF                             ; 
F0DF                             ;  Unchecked build: one byte per character, the low byte of the handler's
F0DF                             ;  distance from PTAB. NPG1 is how many characters, from the start, have
F0DF                             ;  handlers more than 255 bytes past PTAB. ] \ [ @ ? sit where the two ranges
F0DF                             ;  meet (in falling code order for this), and which side each lands on is
F0DF                             ;  worked out here. (One division to a line: asm80 only rounds down when it
F0DF                             ;  stores a value.)
F0DF                             ; 
F0DF                             ;  Checked build: it has more code than the two ranges hold, so its table
F0DF                             ;  holds whole addresses and there are no rules about where handlers go.
F0DF                             ; =============================================================================
F0DF                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                    PGRET:    EQU   (h_ret-PTAB)/256   ; 0 = first range, 1 = second
                    PGBRK:    EQU   (h_break-PTAB)/256   
                    PGDEF:    EQU   (h_def-PTAB)/256   
                    PGFET:    EQU   (h_fetch-PTAB)/256   
                    PGKEY:    EQU   (h_key-PTAB)/256   
                    NPG1:     EQU   20 + PGKEY + PGFET + PGDEF + PGBRK + PGRET   
F0DF                          ENDIF      
F0DF                PTAB:        
F0DF                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              FCB   (h_store-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; !
                              FCB   (h_str-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; "
                              FCB   (h_num-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; #
                              FCB   (h_print-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; $
                              FCB   (h_swap-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; %
                              FCB   (h_and-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; &
                              FCB   (h_emit-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; '
                              FCB   (h_open-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; (
                              FCB   (h_close-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; )
                              FCB   (h_mul-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; *
                              FCB   (h_add-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; +
                              FCB   (h_cfetch-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; ,
                              FCB   (h_sub-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; -
                              FCB   (h_cstore-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; .
                              FCB   (h_div-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; /
                              FCB   (h_dup-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; :
                              FCB   (h_drop-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; ;
                              FCB   (h_lt-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; <
                              FCB   (h_eq-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; =
                              FCB   (h_gt-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; >
                              FCB   (h_key-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; ?
                              FCB   (h_fetch-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; @
                              FCB   (h_def-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; [
                              FCB   (h_break-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; \
                              FCB   (h_ret-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; ]
                              FCB   (h_xor-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; ^
                              FCB   (h_alloc-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; _
                              FCB   (h_grave-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; `
                              FCB   (h_tor-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; {
                              FCB   (h_or-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; |
                              FCB   (h_fromr-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; }
                              FCB   (h_not-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; ~
F0DF                          ENDIF      
F0DF                          IF   CHECKED   
F0DF   F2 BA                  FDB   h_store   ; !
F0E1   F2 44                  FDB   h_str   ; "
F0E3   F2 D4                  FDB   h_num   ; #
F0E5   F2 A6                  FDB   h_print   ; $
F0E7   F2 FA                  FDB   h_swap   ; %
F0E9   F3 06                  FDB   h_and   ; &
F0EB   F2 9F                  FDB   h_emit   ; '
F0ED   F2 3A                  FDB   h_open   ; (
F0EF   F2 5C                  FDB   h_close   ; )
F0F1   F2 69                  FDB   h_mul   ; *
F0F3   F3 0E                  FDB   h_add   ; +
F0F5   F2 54                  FDB   h_cfetch   ; ,
F0F7   F3 15                  FDB   h_sub   ; -
F0F9   F2 C8                  FDB   h_cstore   ; .
F0FB   F3 20                  FDB   h_div   ; /
F0FD   F3 01                  FDB   h_dup   ; :
F0FF   F2 A3                  FDB   h_drop   ; ;
F101   F2 87                  FDB   h_lt   ; <
F103   F2 93                  FDB   h_eq   ; =
F105   F2 85                  FDB   h_gt   ; >
F107   F1 F5                  FDB   h_key   ; ?
F109   F1 EF                  FDB   h_fetch   ; @
F10B   F1 AC                  FDB   h_def   ; [
F10D   F1 9F                  FDB   h_break   ; \
F10F   F1 98                  FDB   h_ret   ; ]
F111   F1 27                  FDB   h_xor   ; ^
F113   F1 45                  FDB   h_alloc   ; _
F115   F1 5E                  FDB   h_grave   ; `
F117   F1 35                  FDB   h_tor   ; {
F119   F1 1F                  FDB   h_or   ; |
F11B   F1 3D                  FDB   h_fromr   ; }
F11D   F1 30                  FDB   h_not   ; ~
F11F                          ENDIF      
F11F                PTABEND:      
F11F                             ; =============================================================================
F11F                             ;  Handlers that must start in the first range (within 255 bytes of PTAB)
F11F                             ;  in the unchecked build: ^ _ ` 00bbIHwg ~
F11F                             ; =============================================================================
F11F   EC C1        H_OR:     LDD   ,U++   
F121   AA C4                  ORA   ,U   
F123   EA 41                  ORB   1,U   
F125   20 06                  BRA   st0   
F127   EC C1        H_XOR:    LDD   ,U++   
F129   A8 C4                  EORA   ,U   
F12B   E8 41                  EORB   1,U   
F12D   ED C4        ST0:      STD   ,U   
F12F   39                     RTS      
F130   63 C4        H_NOT:    COM   ,U   
F132   63 41                  COM   1,U   
F134   39                     RTS      
F135                             ; "{" ( n -- ) R: ( -- n )     The dispatcher's return address comes off the
F135                             ; return stack first (PULS X) and is jumped to at the end.
F135   35 10        H_TOR:    PULS   X   
F137   37 06                  PULU   D   
F139   34 06                  PSHS   D   
F13B   6E 84                  JMP   ,X   
F13D                             ; "}" ( -- n ) R: ( n -- )
F13D   35 10        H_FROMR:   PULS   X   
F13F   35 06                  PULS   D   
F141   36 06                  PSHU   D   
F143   6E 84                  JMP   ,X   
F145                             ; "_" ( n -- addr ): the heap pointer moves up by n; TOS is the old pointer.
F145   D6 7C        H_ALLOC:   LDB   <HEAP   
F147   96 7D                  LDA   <HEAP+1   
F149   1F 01                  TFR   D,X   ; the old pointer
F14B   E3 C4                  ADDD   ,U   
F14D                          IF   CHECKED   
F14D   10 25 FE B8            LBCS   e_heap   ; a negative count wraps: too big
F151   81 F0                  CMPA   #HEAPLIM   
F153   10 24 FE B2            LBHS   e_heap   ; the new top must stay below the limit page
F157                          ENDIF      
F157   D7 7C                  STB   <HEAP   
F159   97 7D                  STA   <HEAP+1   
F15B   AF C4                  STX   ,U   
F15D   39                     RTS      
F15E                             ; ---- machine code: the grave -----------------------------------------------
F15E                             ; "`" plus a hex digit loads bytes: ( addr -- addr' ). Pairs of hex digits
F15E                             ; are stored from addr until a non-hex character; then a RTS (39h) is
F15E                             ; written and its address is left. An odd last digit is consumed and dropped.
F15E                             ; "`" plus anything else calls the machine code at TOS: ( addr -- ). The
F15E                             ; code is entered by JSR (the dispatcher's own), with the address already
F15E                             ; popped: U points at the top data cell (big-endian, 2 bytes, stack grows
F15E                             ; down) and the return address is on top of S. The code may pop and push
F15E                             ; data cells by changing U; on return the cell at ,U is the new TOS. It must
F15E                             ; keep Y (the interpreter's reading position), DP and S (balanced), and
F15E                             ; return with RTS. A, B, X, CC may change.
F15E   8D 26        H_GRAVE:   BSR   hexc   ; the digit after the grave, if any
F160   24 20                  BCC   exec   
F162   AE C4                  LDX   ,U   
F164   C6 10        HX1:      LDB   #16   
F166   3D                     MUL      ; B = the digit, moved up to the high half
F167                          IF   CHECKED   
F167   BD F3 73               JSR   chkst   
F16A                          ENDIF      
F16A   E7 84                  STB   ,X   ; (an odd digit is overwritten by the RTS)
F16C   8D 18                  BSR   hexc   
F16E   24 08                  BCC   hx2   ; odd digit: already consumed, dropped
F170   AA 84                  ORA   ,X   
F172   A7 80                  STA   ,X+   
F174   8D 10                  BSR   hexc   
F176   25 EC                  BCS   hx1   
F178                HX2:         
F178                          IF   CHECKED   
F178   BD F3 73               JSR   chkst   
F17B                          ENDIF      
F17B   86 39                  LDA   #39h   ; RTS
F17D   A7 84                  STA   ,X   
F17F   AF C4                  STX   ,U   
F181   39                     RTS      
F182   AE C1        EXEC:     LDX   ,U++   
F184   6E 84                  JMP   ,X   ; the code's RTS returns to the dispatcher
F186                             ; hexc: if the character at IP is a hex digit (0-9, A-F, a-f), step over it
F186                             ; and return its value in A with the carry set; otherwise leave the IP and
F186                             ; return with the carry clear.
F186   BD F0 BA     HEXC:     JSR   isdig   
F189   25 0A                  BLO   hv1   ; C = 1
F18B   84 DF                  ANDA   #0DFh   
F18D   80 11                  SUBA   #11h   
F18F   81 06                  CMPA   #6   
F191   24 04                  BHS   hv9   ; C = 0
F193   80 F6                  SUBA   #0F6h   ; + 10, and sets the carry
F195   31 21        HV1:      LEAY   1,Y   ; (LEAY leaves the carry alone)
F197   39           HV9:      RTS      
F198                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                    GETK:     EQU   KEY   ; the host's routine does the whole job
F198                          ENDIF      
F198                             ; ---- where the two ranges meet ---------------------------------------------
F198                             ; The first range ends somewhere among the next five handlers, ] \ [ @ ?
F198                             ; (they are in falling code order for this): NPG1 follows. Every handler
F198                             ; below them must start in the second range, and every one above in the
F198                             ; first.
F198                             ; "]" returns: pop an address and jump to it. (PULS X,Y: the dispatcher's
F198                             ; return address into X, then the saved IP into Y.)
F198                H_RET:       
F198                          IF   CHECKED   
F198   BD F3 80               JSR   chkbrk   ; Ctrl-C is checked at every word return
F19B                          ENDIF      
F19B   35 30                  PULS   X,Y   
F19D   6E 84                  JMP   ,X   
F19F                             ; "\" ( flag -- ): true skips to the next ")" or "]" at this level; ")"
F19F                             ; drops the block start, "]" returns. No closer at all ends the program.
F19F   EC C1        H_BREAK:   LDD   ,U++   
F1A1   27 48                  BEQ   sk9   ; false: nothing to do
F1A3   8D 27                  BSR   skip   
F1A5   4D                     TSTA      ; skip returns 0 for ")"
F1A6   26 F0                  BNE   h_ret   
F1A8   35 16        RDROP:    PULS   D,X   ; the return address and the block start
F1AA   1F 05                  TFR   D,PC   ; back to the dispatcher
F1AC                             ; "[" followed by a letter stores the body"s address in that letter"s cell:
F1AC                             ; uppercase is a word, lowercase a variable. Followed by a space it pushes
F1AC                             ; the body"s address instead. Either way it then skips to the matching "]'.
F1AC                             ; (The unchecked build takes anything below "A" as the space, and anything
F1AC                             ; from "A" up as a letter.)
F1AC   A6 A0        H_DEF:    LDA   ,Y+   
F1AE                          IF   CHECKED   
F1AE   81 20                  CMPA   #" "   
F1B0   27 18                  BEQ   def2   
F1B2   1F 89                  TFR   A,B   
F1B4   C4 DF                  ANDB   #0DFh   ; fold case
F1B6   C0 41                  SUBB   #"A"   
F1B8   C1 1A                  CMPB   #26   
F1BA   10 24 FE 51            LBHS   e_brack   ; anything but a letter or a space
F1BE                          ENDIF      
F1BE   80 41                  SUBA   #"A"   ; 0-25 or 32-57: lowercase lands 64 bytes up
F1C0                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              BLO   def2   
F1C0                          ENDIF      
F1C0   BD F0 B3               JSR   cellx   
F1C3   1F 20                  TFR   Y,D   
F1C5   E7 84                  STB   ,X   ; little-endian
F1C7   A7 01                  STA   1,X   
F1C9   8C                     FCB   8Ch   ; (CMPX #: steps over the PSHU)
F1CA   36 20        DEF2:     PSHU   Y   ; an anonymous block: push its address
F1CC                             ; fall into skip
F1CC                             ; skip: read past text to the closer at this level, and return A = 0 if it
F1CC                             ; was ")" and 2 if it was "]". Brackets of both kinds count together;
F1CC                             ; strings are stepped over whole. A NUL first ends the program (for "\" with
F1CC                             ; no closer; anything else that runs into the NUL had unbalanced brackets
F1CC                             ; anyway). B counts the open levels.
F1CC   5F           SKIP:     CLRB      
F1CD   A6 A0        SK1:      LDA   ,Y+   
F1CF   10 27 FE 61            LBEQ   fin   
F1D3   81 22                  CMPA   #22h   
F1D5   26 02                  BNE   sk2   
F1D7   8D 70                  BSR   skipstr   ; leaves A = 22h, which matches nothing below
F1D9   80 28        SK2:      SUBA   #"("   
F1DB   27 0F                  BEQ   sk3   
F1DD   4A                     DECA      ; ")"
F1DE   27 08                  BEQ   sk4   
F1E0   80 32                  SUBA   #"["-")"   
F1E2   27 08                  BEQ   sk3   
F1E4   81 02                  CMPA   #"]"-"["   
F1E6   26 E5                  BNE   sk1   
F1E8   5A           SK4:      DECB      
F1E9   2A E2                  BPL   sk1   
F1EB   39           SK9:      RTS      ; the closer at this level
F1EC   5C           SK3:      INCB      
F1ED   20 DE                  BRA   sk1   
F1EF   AE C4        H_FETCH:   LDX   ,U   ; "@" (the cell in memory is little-endian)
F1F1   A6 01                  LDA   1,X   
F1F3   20 62                  BRA   cf1   
F1F5                             ; "?" ( n -- c ) or ( -n -- addr )
F1F5                             ;   n > 0: wait about n ms for a key; 0 if none came
F1F5                             ;   n = 0: wait for a key
F1F5                             ;   n < 0: read a line of at most -n characters, with echo. n is not
F1F5                             ;          checked: the buffer holds 127 characters and the CR, so a
F1F5                             ;          program must ask for 127 or fewer.
F1F5   AE C4        H_KEY:    LDX   ,U   
F1F7   2B 17                  BMI   line   
F1F9   C6 14        KT1:      LDB   #MSLOOP   ; one millisecond, roughly
F1FB   BD F3 8D     KT2:      JSR   getk   
F1FE   26 0B                  BNE   kt3   
F200   5A                     DECB      
F201   26 F8                  BNE   kt2   
F203   30 1F                  LEAX   -1,X   
F205   26 F2                  BNE   kt1   ; A = 0 if the time ran out
F207   AE C4                  LDX   ,U   ; 0?: the countdown from 0 took 65536 ms;
F209   27 EE                  BEQ   kt1   ;   run it again, until a key comes
F20B   6F C4        KT3:      CLR   ,U   
F20D   A7 41                  STA   1,U   
F20F   39                     RTS      
F210                             ; Backspace takes the last character back (and is echoed as it is), CR ends
F210                             ; (stored, not echoed), every other key is stored and echoed until the line
F210                             ; is full. B = the length so far; the low byte of the top cell becomes the
F210                             ; most allowed (it holds minus the count on entry).
F210   60 41        LINE:     NEG   1,U   
F212   8E 82 80               LDX   #LINEBUF   
F215   5F                     CLRB      
F216   BD F3 8D     LN2:      JSR   getk   
F219   27 FB                  BEQ   ln2   
F21B   81 0D                  CMPA   #13   
F21D   27 16                  BEQ   ln5   
F21F   81 08                  CMPA   #8   
F221   27 0C                  BEQ   ln4   
F223   E1 41                  CMPB   1,U   
F225   24 EF                  BHS   ln2   ; full
F227   A7 85                  STA   B,X   
F229   5C                     INCB      
F22A   BD FF 03     LN3:      JSR   CONOUT   
F22D   20 E7                  BRA   ln2   
F22F   5D           LN4:      TSTB      ; Backspace: nothing to take back?
F230   27 E4                  BEQ   ln2   
F232   5A                     DECB      
F233   20 F5                  BRA   ln3   ; echo it
F235   A7 85        LN5:      STA   B,X   ; A = 13
F237   AF C4                  STX   ,U   
F239   39                     RTS      
F23A                             ; =============================================================================
F23A                             ;  Handlers that must start in the second range (unchecked build).
F23A                             ; =============================================================================
F23A                             ; "(" ( flag -- ): true pushes the block start and enters; false skips to
F23A                             ; the matching ")".
F23A   EC C1        H_OPEN:   LDD   ,U++   
F23C   27 8E                  BEQ   skip   ; tail call: skip ends in RTS
F23E   35 10                  PULS   X   
F240   34 20                  PSHS   Y   
F242   6E 84                  JMP   ,X   
F244                             ; 22h pushes the address of the text after it and skips the string.
F244   36 20        H_STR:    PSHU   Y   
F246   8C                     FCB   8Ch   ; (CMPX #: steps over the LEAY)
F247                             ; skipstr: IP is inside a string; step past its closing quote. "/" escapes
F247                             ; the next character, so "/"" does not end it. Leaves A = 22h.
F247   31 21        SS0:      LEAY   1,Y   
F249   A6 A0        SKIPSTR:   LDA   ,Y+   
F24B   81 2F                  CMPA   #"/"   
F24D   27 F8                  BEQ   ss0   
F24F   81 22                  CMPA   #22h   
F251   26 F6                  BNE   skipstr   
F253   39                     RTS      
F254   AE C4        H_CFETCH:   LDX   ,U   ; ","
F256   4F                     CLRA      
F257   E6 84        CF1:      LDB   ,X   
F259   ED C4                  STD   ,U   
F25B   39                     RTS      
F25C                             ; ")" ( flag -- ): true jumps back to the block start (and keeps it); false
F25C                             ; drops it and carries on.
F25C   EC C1        H_CLOSE:   LDD   ,U++   
F25E   10 27 FF 46            LBEQ   rdrop   
F262                          IF   CHECKED   
F262   BD F3 80               JSR   chkbrk   ; Ctrl-C is checked at every loop-back
F265                          ENDIF      
F265   10 AE 62               LDY   2,S   ; the block start, under the return address
F268   39                     RTS      
F269                             ; ---- arithmetic and logic: ( NOS TOS -- result ) ---------------------------
F269                             ; "*": three 8x8 multiplies; only the low 16 bits are kept.
F269                             ; a = ah:al at 2,U.  b = bh:bl at ,U.
F269   A6 43        H_MUL:    LDA   3,U   
F26B   E6 C4                  LDB   ,U   
F26D   3D                     MUL      ; al*bh
F26E   E7 C4                  STB   ,U   ; (bh is no longer needed)
F270   A6 42                  LDA   2,U   
F272   E6 41                  LDB   1,U   
F274   3D                     MUL      ; ah*bl
F275   EB C4                  ADDB   ,U   
F277   E7 C4                  STB   ,U   ; the cross terms, low byte
F279   A6 43                  LDA   3,U   
F27B   E6 41                  LDB   1,U   
F27D   3D                     MUL      ; al*bl
F27E   AB C4                  ADDA   ,U   
F280   33 42                  LEAU   2,U   
F282   ED C4                  STD   ,U   
F284   39                     RTS      
F285                             ; Signed compares: a-b, then a branch to put -1 or 0 on the stack.
F285   8D 73        H_GT:     BSR   h_swap   ; a > b is b < a
F287   8D 10        H_LT:     BSR   cmp   
F289   2D 02                  BLT   true   
F28B   5F           FALSE:    CLRB      
F28C   8C                     FCB   8Ch   ; (CMPX #: steps over the LDB)
F28D   C6 FF        TRUE:     LDB   #0FFh   
F28F   1D                     SEX      ; D = 0000 or FFFF
F290   ED C4                  STD   ,U   
F292   39                     RTS      
F293   8D 04        H_EQ:     BSR   cmp   
F295   27 F6                  BEQ   true   
F297   20 F2                  BRA   false   
F299   EC 42        CMP:      LDD   2,U   
F29B   10 A3 C1               CMPD   ,U++   
F29E   39                     RTS      
F29F   A6 41        H_EMIT:   LDA   1,U   ; "'"
F2A1   8D 54                  BSR   putc   
F2A3   33 42        H_DROP:   LEAU   2,U   ; ";"
F2A5   39                     RTS      
F2A6                             ; "$" prints the string at TOS, decoding escapes: "/" plus a character
F2A6                             ; clears that character"s bit 6 (/M is CR, /` is space; "/" and ""' have no
F2A6                             ; bit 6, so // and /" give themselves).
F2A6   AE C4        H_PRINT:   LDX   ,U   
F2A8   A6 80        PR0:      LDA   ,X+   
F2AA   81 22                  CMPA   #22h   
F2AC   27 F5                  BEQ   h_drop   
F2AE   81 2F                  CMPA   #"/"   
F2B0   26 04                  BNE   pr1   
F2B2   A6 80                  LDA   ,X+   
F2B4   84 BF                  ANDA   #0BFh   
F2B6   8D 3F        PR1:      BSR   putc   
F2B8   20 EE                  BRA   pr0   
F2BA                             ; "!" ( n addr -- ) is "." with the high byte stored first. The cell in
F2BA                             ; memory is little-endian.
F2BA   AE C4        H_STORE:   LDX   ,U   
F2BC                          IF   CHECKED   
F2BC   30 01                  LEAX   1,X   ; both bytes must be in the program's space
F2BE   BD F3 73               JSR   chkst   
F2C1   30 1F                  LEAX   -1,X   
F2C3                          ENDIF      
F2C3   A6 42                  LDA   2,U   
F2C5   A7 01                  STA   1,X   
F2C7   8C                     FCB   8Ch   ; (CMPX #: steps over the LDX)
F2C8   AE C4        H_CSTORE:   LDX   ,U   ; "." ( c addr -- )
F2CA                          IF   CHECKED   
F2CA   BD F3 73               JSR   chkst   
F2CD                          ENDIF      
F2CD   33 42                  LEAU   2,U   
F2CF   37 06                  PULU   D   
F2D1   E7 84                  STB   ,X   
F2D3   39                     RTS      
F2D4                             ; "#" prints TOS as a signed decimal number, with no space after it.
F2D4   6D C4        H_NUM:    TST   ,U   
F2D6   2A 06                  BPL   pdec   
F2D8   86 2D                  LDA   #"-"   
F2DA   8D 1B                  BSR   putc   
F2DC   8D 69                  BSR   negt   
F2DE                             ; pdec: print the top cell as unsigned and drop it, by recursion on /10
F2DE   CC 00 0A     PDEC:     LDD   #10   
F2E1   36 06                  PSHU   D   
F2E3   8D 73                  BSR   udiv   ; NOS = quotient, TOS = digit
F2E5   37 06                  PULU   D   ; the digit
F2E7   34 04                  PSHS   B   
F2E9   EC C4                  LDD   ,U   
F2EB   27 04                  BEQ   pd1   
F2ED   8D EF                  BSR   pdec   
F2EF   20 02                  BRA   pd2   
F2F1   33 42        PD1:      LEAU   2,U   ; drop the zero quotient
F2F3   35 02        PD2:      PULS   A   
F2F5   8B 30                  ADDA   #"0"   ; and fall into putc
F2F7   7E FF 03     PUTC:     JMP   CONOUT   
F2FA                             ; ---- stack and storage -----------------------------------------------------
F2FA   37 16        H_SWAP:   PULU   D,X   ; "%"
F2FC   36 06                  PSHU   D   
F2FE   36 10                  PSHU   X   
F300   39                     RTS      
F301   EC C4        H_DUP:    LDD   ,U   ; ":"
F303   36 06                  PSHU   D   
F305   39                     RTS      
F306   EC C1        H_AND:    LDD   ,U++   
F308   A4 C4                  ANDA   ,U   
F30A   E4 41                  ANDB   1,U   
F30C   20 04                  BRA   st   
F30E   EC C1        H_ADD:    LDD   ,U++   
F310   E3 C4                  ADDD   ,U   
F312   ED C4        ST:       STD   ,U   
F314   39                     RTS      
F315                             ; "-" has two jobs: directly before a digit it starts a negative number.
F315   BD F0 BA     H_SUB:    JSR   isdig   
F318   25 2A                  BLO   negnum   
F31A   EC 42                  LDD   2,U   
F31C   A3 C1                  SUBD   ,U++   
F31E   20 F2                  BRA   st   
F320                             ; ---- the tail ---------------------------------------------------------------
F320                             ; "/" is the last handler, so what follows its first byte may lie past the
F320                             ; second range: the divide itself and the routines after it.
F320                             ; "/" ( a b -- r q ): the quotient is on top. Truncates toward zero; r takes
F320                             ; a's sign. Divide |a| by |b|, then q gets the sign of a XOR b and r the sign
F320                             ; of a. Dividing by zero is not checked: it returns two cells of no meaning.
F320   A6 42        H_DIV:    LDA   2,U   
F322   34 02                  PSHS   A   ; a's sign: for r
F324   A8 C4                  EORA   ,U   
F326   34 02                  PSHS   A   ; a xor b: for q
F328   30 42                  LEAX   2,U   
F32A   8D 26                  BSR   absx   ; |a|
F32C   1F 31                  TFR   U,X   
F32E   8D 22                  BSR   absx   ; |b|
F330   8D 26                  BSR   udiv   ; NOS = q, TOS = r
F332   8D C6                  BSR   h_swap   ; NOS = r, TOS = q
F334   1F 31                  TFR   U,X   
F336   6D E0                  TST   ,S+   
F338   2A 02                  BPL   dv1   
F33A   8D 0D                  BSR   negx   ; q's sign
F33C   30 42        DV1:      LEAX   2,U   
F33E   6D E0                  TST   ,S+   
F340   2A 0F                  BPL   ng9   
F342   20 05                  BRA   negx   ; r's sign
F344   BD F0 C1     NEGNUM:   JSR   rdnum   ; a negative literal: read it, then negate
F347   1F 31        NEGT:     TFR   U,X   
F349   EC 84        NEGX:     LDD   ,X   ; negx: negate the cell at X
F34B   40                     NEGA      
F34C   50                     NEGB      
F34D   82 00                  SBCA   #0   
F34F   ED 84                  STD   ,X   
F351   39           NG9:      RTS      
F352   6D 84        ABSX:     TST   ,X   ; absx: negate the cell at X if negative
F354   2A FB                  BPL   ng9   
F356   20 F1                  BRA   negx   
F358                             ; udiv: unsigned divide, in place. The dividend is the NOS cell and the
F358                             ; divisor the TOS cell, both <= 8000h; the NOS cell becomes the quotient and
F358                             ; the TOS cell the remainder. The remainder is built in D (always < the
F358                             ; divisor, so 2R+1 fits in 16 bits).
F358   8E 00 10     UDIV:     LDX   #16   
F35B   4F                     CLRA      
F35C   5F                     CLRB      
F35D   68 43        UD1:      ASL   3,U   
F35F   69 42                  ROL   2,U   ; the dividend's top bit ...
F361   59                     ROLB      
F362   49                     ROLA      ; ... into the remainder
F363   10 A3 C4               CMPD   ,U   
F366   25 04                  BLO   ud2   
F368   A3 C4                  SUBD   ,U   
F36A   6C 43                  INC   3,U   ; a quotient bit
F36C   30 1F        UD2:      LEAX   -1,X   
F36E   26 ED                  BNE   ud1   
F370   ED C4                  STD   ,U   
F372   39                     RTS      
F373                          IF   CHECKED   
F373                             ; chkst: stop unless X is in the program's own space: from the letter page
F373                             ; up to HEAPLIM, so the interpreter's stacks and whatever lies above the
F373                             ; limit are safe. Memory above the heap top but below the limit is the
F373                             ; program's own: Tiny BASIC keeps its lines there. Keeps every register.
F373   8C 82 00     CHKST:    CMPX   #LET   
F376   25 05                  BLO   cs9   
F378   8C F0 00               CMPX   #HEAPLIM*256   
F37B   25 17                  BLO   gk9   ; in range: return
F37D   7E F0 0C     CS9:      JMP   e_store   
F380                             ; chkbrk: a waiting key is read now; Ctrl-C stops the program, anything
F380                             ; else is held for the next "?".
F380   8D 0B        CHKBRK:   BSR   getk   
F382   27 10                  BEQ   gk9   
F384   81 03                  CMPA   #3   
F386   10 27 FC 7C            LBEQ   e_break   
F38A   97 34                  STA   <KEYBUF   
F38C   39                     RTS      
F38D                             ; getk: a key held back by the break check goes first; then the host's KEY.
F38D   96 34        GETK:     LDA   <KEYBUF   
F38F   27 04                  BEQ   gk1   
F391   0F 34                  CLR   <KEYBUF   
F393   4D                     TSTA      
F394   39           GK9:      RTS      
F395   7E FF 06     GK1:      JMP   KEY   
F398                          ENDIF      
